# EAS Build archives the whole monorepo by default (git root, not the
# project directory). The first attempt at trimming this excluded entire
# backend service directories, which broke `pnpm install` — this is a pnpm
# workspace, and pnpm needs every workspace member's package.json present to
# resolve the shared lockfile, even services the mobile app never imports
# from. This version is narrower: it only excludes files that are never
# needed to install dependencies or build the app, never whole app trees.
#
# The single biggest offender by far is Prisma's generated native query
# engines — compiled binaries for every OS (Windows .dll.node, macOS
# .dylib.node, Linux .so.node), ~16–19MB each, duplicated across seven
# backend services and committed to git. They're pure build output
# (regenerated by `prisma generate`) and irrelevant to installing packages
# or building an Expo app.
**/prisma/generated/*.node
**/prisma/generated/*.node.tmp*

# Compiled Go binaries — also build output, also git-tracked, also
# irrelevant here.
apps/scheduling-service/server
apps/scheduling-service/server.exe

# Docs, ML models/exports, test fixtures, the Python agent tier, and Firebase
# hosting config — safe because they are files, not workspace members; no
# package.json anywhere under these ever appears in pnpm-workspace.yaml.
docs/
models/
exports/
tests/
agent/
api/
analytics/
scripts/
.firebase/
firebase.json
.firebaserc
